      "text": "Neither can any natural man abide the presence of God, D&C 67:12. These shall dwell in the presence of God, D&C 76:62. they who receive of the presence of the Son, D&C 76:77. They who dwell in his presence are the church of the Firstborn, D&C 76:94. they may be able to bear his presence, D&C 76:118. hardened their hearts and could not endure his presence, D&C 84:24. my glory … and my presence shall be there, D&C 94:8 (97:16). angels shall go up before you, and also my presence, D&C 103:20. enjoy the communion and presence of God the Father, D&C 107:19. every man shall enter into his eternal presence, D&C 121:32. shall thy confidence wax strong in the presence of God, D&C 121:45. presence of God, on a globe like a sea of glass, D&C 130:7. sanctified … to dwell in his presence, D&C 133:35.",
